blob: f2a33cfac0199fe80bc95047ce04c0b540dd0415
decision: pass
reviewer: claude-opus-5-5 (self-review)
audience: Maintainers of the standard and adopting-project leads
purpose: How should unresolved items from a change be linked and closed?

docs/design/0003-unresolved-item-ledger.md is a draft design proposal; it concludes that anything a change cannot close is linked to a tracked work item with one owner and a person-judgeable closing condition, and that a third verdict ("does the explanation still hold after later changes") stays separate from editorial review.
Translated from Korean in full: summary, ownership table, five kinds of unresolved items, work item form, five-step change handling, periodic check scope, what was implemented first, first operating targets. Frontmatter, links, paths and identifiers are unchanged.
Korean kept on purpose: the tracker-body example code block (a literal example as a Korean-language project writes it), the MR section name `영향 및 후속 작업` (a contract value), and the blockquoted MR section example. Each has an English rendering next to it.
Historical facts (the two 2026-09-10 cases, ADR 0024 implementation, public-ai-qa preconditions) were not updated to the current implementation.
Reread as an English reader and compared against HEAD; no facts, conditions or numbers dropped. Limitation: self-review by the translator, not an independent reader.

